 network demonstrates strong chemical realism but is not currently APPROVED (overall_confidence < 0.9) until mass and charge conservation is enforced in all reactions.\"\n}", "parsed_response": {"pathway_evaluations": [{"pathway_id": "P1", "reaction_scores": {"rxn_001": 0.6, "rxn_002": 0.6, "rxn_003": 0.8}, "chemical_feasibility": 0.65, "pathway_coherence": 1.0, "environmental_progression": 1.0, "target_achievement": 1.0, "overall_confidence": 0.85, "feedback": "The cyanosulfidic Pathway 1 accurately reflects the three-step synthesis of threonine outlined in Patel et al. (2015) and is strongly supported by literature, both in sequence and environmental context. However, reactions rxn_001 and rxn_002 are unbalanced as written (missing elements/species per the atom/charge check, e.g. O2/H2 as byproducts), indicating mass conservation issues in the network implementation even though the intended chemistry is valid. Reaction rxn_003 is only balanceable with correct water/ammonia stoichiometry. Adjusting the reaction equations to explicitly list all mass-balance-conserving species (H2O, O2, H2 as shown in the balance check) would raise feasibility to excellent. Despite these specification flaws, the mechanistic and environmental aspects are robust.", "approved": true, "problematic_reactions": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002"], "suggestions": ["Explicitly balance rxn_001 (add O2 or H2 as necessary)", "Explicitly balance rxn_002 (consider CO2/CO/HCN/H2 as side products as needed)", "Review all product/reactant lists for atom conservation."]}, {"pathway_id": "P2", "reaction_scores": {"rxn_004": 0.6}, "chemical_feasibility": 0.6, "pathway_coherence": 0.95, "environmental_progression": 1.0, "target_achievement": 1.0, "overall_confidence": 0.8, "feedback": "This pathway mirrors the literature-documented hydrothermal alanine-formaldehyde aldol condensation to threonine (Aubrey et al., 2008). However, the reaction as written (rxn_004) is unbalanced (missing H2O or byproduct), negatively im